WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:02.980
SPEAKER: You've got a great
idea for the next big app,

00:00:02.980 --> 00:00:04.970
and you're just
itching to get started.

00:00:04.970 --> 00:00:07.550
You want a development
platform that's easy to use,

00:00:07.550 --> 00:00:09.550
and you want to make sure
it's going to scale up

00:00:09.550 --> 00:00:11.120
with you after you make it big.

00:00:11.120 --> 00:00:13.260
You want to pick the language
you're most comfortable with.

00:00:13.260 --> 00:00:15.926
And of course, you don't want to
think too much about monitoring

00:00:15.926 --> 00:00:17.060
and operations.

00:00:17.060 --> 00:00:20.060
Well, it's time to check
out Google App Engine.

00:00:20.060 --> 00:00:22.340
App Engine is a managed
application platform

00:00:22.340 --> 00:00:24.500
that supports any
language, framework,

00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:26.480
or library you want to use.

00:00:26.480 --> 00:00:28.110
We worry about the
infrastructure,

00:00:28.110 --> 00:00:30.140
so you can focus on your code.

00:00:30.140 --> 00:00:34.730
You can get started today with
Node.js, Ruby, PHP, Go, Java,

00:00:34.730 --> 00:00:36.830
Python, or even .NET.

00:00:36.830 --> 00:00:39.230
And if that's not enough,
you can bring your own custom

00:00:39.230 --> 00:00:43.362
container using any programming
language or library.

00:00:43.362 --> 00:00:45.070
When you're ready to
deploy to the cloud,

00:00:45.070 --> 00:00:47.250
just run gcloud app deploy.

00:00:47.250 --> 00:00:49.250
App Engine will take care
of uploading your code

00:00:49.250 --> 00:00:51.860
and running it on
Google's infrastructure.

00:00:51.860 --> 00:00:53.990
For Java or .NET
lovers out there,

00:00:53.990 --> 00:00:56.510
we have great integration
with Eclipse, IntelliJ,

00:00:56.510 --> 00:01:00.340
and Visual Studio, making
it simple to get started.

00:01:00.340 --> 00:01:02.590
When you're ready to push
updates to your application,

00:01:02.590 --> 00:01:04.329
App Engine makes it easy.

00:01:04.329 --> 00:01:06.370
You can run multiple
versions of your application

00:01:06.370 --> 00:01:08.710
at the same time
and can even split

00:01:08.710 --> 00:01:11.180
traffic between different
versions of your app,

00:01:11.180 --> 00:01:14.770
making it simple to perform
rollouts or A/B testing.

00:01:14.770 --> 00:01:16.360
As your application
starts to grow,

00:01:16.360 --> 00:01:18.940
we'll automatically
scale it for you.

00:01:18.940 --> 00:01:20.620
App Engine
automatically balances

00:01:20.620 --> 00:01:23.470
instances of your application
across multiple availability

00:01:23.470 --> 00:01:26.660
zones, making sure your
app is up and available.

00:01:26.660 --> 00:01:28.240
And if your traffic
slows down, we'll

00:01:28.240 --> 00:01:32.110
automatically scale the number
of instances back down as well.

00:01:32.110 --> 00:01:34.640
Of course, no one
writes perfect code.

00:01:34.640 --> 00:01:37.000
Being able to debug and
monitor applications,

00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:41.140
even in production, is just as
important as deploying code.

00:01:41.140 --> 00:01:43.900
App Engine integrates seamlessly
with Google Stackdriver

00:01:43.900 --> 00:01:45.220
diagnostics.

00:01:45.220 --> 00:01:47.890
Monitoring, logging,
debugging, tracing--

00:01:47.890 --> 00:01:50.800
it's all available out of
the box with minimal setup

00:01:50.800 --> 00:01:52.870
and configuration.

00:01:52.870 --> 00:01:55.240
Running your code in the
cloud is just a start.

00:01:55.240 --> 00:01:58.540
You need databases, caches,
scalable file storage.

00:01:58.540 --> 00:02:01.690
And here's where the rest of
Google Cloud Platform comes in.

00:02:01.690 --> 00:02:04.090
App Engine lets you leverage
these powerful systems

00:02:04.090 --> 00:02:07.810
without needing to worry
about setup or infrastructure.

00:02:07.810 --> 00:02:09.400
Our goal with App
Engine is to make

00:02:09.400 --> 00:02:12.850
developing applications for the
cloud just a little bit easier.

00:02:12.850 --> 00:02:15.220
You bring the code, and
we'll handle the rest.

00:02:15.220 --> 00:02:17.940
I can't wait to see
what you'll build next.

